{
  "comment": "Agent SoW signatures bound to seats (agentsow.com 0.26.0-draft, 5.1 and 6). Every seat carries owner_key, and a signature record counts for its seat only when its key is that owner_key, the registry's owner of the seat's agent is that same key, and its signature verifies over the signed bytes: 'agent-sow-v1', one newline, the JCS of the document minus signatures. owner_key sits inside the signed bytes, so a seat's key cannot change after signing without breaking every signature. The document is the cross-SDK document of sow-pricing.json (signing.document) with owner_key added to both seats. The keys are derived from the published seeds below (each seed is the SHA-256 of its label), each sig is the padded base64 of the 64-byte Ed25519 signature, and Ed25519 is deterministic, so any implementation reproduces them. The seeds are public by design and sign nothing else. THE FIXTURE IS THE AUTHORITY: change it only with a spec change alongside.",
  "version": 1,
